#
# Counter-example for math:UnderspecifiedEstimateShape: a math:Estimate that DOES name its
# math:Estimand through math:estimatesEstimand (so the sh:or target arm is satisfied) and
# carries its value through math:estimateValue, but names NO math:Estimator through
# math:estimator — a produced value with no procedure, a bare number without its act. It
# fails ONLY the estimator min-count property of math:UnderspecifiedEstimateShape (the
# sh:or is satisfied by the estimand, so it does not trip), so validation MUST emit
# shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding (math:UnderspecifiedEstimate). No
# other shape targets a math:Estimate, math:Estimand, or the untyped value node.
# Bound by ex:ecEstimateNoEstimator.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:treatmentEffectEstimate a math:Estimate ;
    math:estimatesEstimand ex:averageTreatmentEffect ;
    math:estimateValue ex:effectValue .

ex:averageTreatmentEffect a math:Estimand .
